// Read-only lookup of the approval record in Tamsora. It needs its own permit,
// otherwise the call is recorded as an error and never as a response.
@id("allow-tamsora-get-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Tamsora___get_approval", resource);

// Closing is allowed only at MAIN, and only if this session recently saw a
// completed Tamsora lookup showing that this exact work order (same site and
// wonum) was ACCEPTED by a PERSON within the last hour.
@id("allow-close-main-with-human-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Tamsora___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    output.decision: "ACCEPTED",
    output.approver_kind: "PERSON"
  }
};
```

- **Unverified vocabulary:** Tamsora declares `decision` and `approver_kind` as plain strings, with no enum. I used `"ACCEPTED"` and `"PERSON"`, matching the sibling Ostrel schema, whose enums include REFUSED/OPEN for the rejected and still-open cases. Please confirm these are Tamsora's actual values.
- **Closing:** It is allowed only at MAIN, and only on a completed lookup (`::response`) from this session. Failed or denied lookups are recorded as errors and so never match.
- **No self-approval:** `approve_workorder` has no permit, so it is denied by default. `Ostrel___get_approval` is also unpermitted, since Tamsora is the system of record for approvals. Every other tool is denied as well.

